//! Stack navigation for Loom: screens pushed onto a [`Stack`] and popped off it, as a native
//! app's navigation controller or React Navigation's stack does.
//!
//! A screen is a model that implements [`Screen`]: its own messages, commands, view and
//! subscriptions. The stack is a value in the app's model. A screen moves the stack by
//! reporting an [`Action`] from its `update`; the stack starts the new screen's commands under
//! the screen's key, and cancels them when the screen leaves.
//!
//! Every screen on the stack stays live until it leaves: it keeps its model and its nodes
//! (scroll, focus), its subscriptions run and its commands finish. A screen that another one
//! fully covers is not drawn, and its view is not rebuilt until it shows again.
pub import stack {
  Stack,
  Screen,
  Action,
  Presentation,
  Message,
  Owned,
  Out,
  Entry
}
pub import header { header }
